# Globe rendering

Read `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` and `docs/PERFORMANCE.md` before editing.

- Keep frame-level state in R3F/Three.js refs — not React state or Zustand.
- No object creation inside `useFrame` unless unavoidable; reuse vectors, colors, quaternions.
- Prefer `BufferGeometry`. Reuse materials and textures.
- Do not render one React DOM element per country.
- Avoid per-country React component trees when geometry can be batched.
- Picking/hover must not trigger broad React re-renders every frame.
- Respect quality tiers and DPR caps from `docs/PERFORMANCE.md`.
- Atmosphere, stars, and post-processing are progressive enhancement — core interaction must work without them.
- WebGL failure must degrade gracefully (see `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`).

Visual tuning: `docs/DESIGN.md` (restrained, globe remains dominant).
